---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { centersByRegion, allColleges, stats, formatNumber, withThe, KOSHER_KEYS } from '../../lib/centers';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const path = '/jewish-life-on-campus/florida/';
const regions = centersByRegion();
const colleges = allColleges();
const biggest = colleges
  .filter((r) => r.campus.jewishStudents)
  .sort((a, b) => (b.campus.jewishStudents || 0) - (a.campus.jewishStudents || 0))
  .slice(0, 8);
const regionCopy: Record<string, string> = {
  north:
    'North Florida is home to two of the state\'s largest universities. Gainesville has one of the largest Jewish student communities in the country at the University of Florida, Tallahassee brings together students from Florida State, FAMU and Tallahassee Community College, and Jacksonville\'s Chabad serves UNF, Jacksonville University and FSCJ.',
  central:
    'Orlando is anchored by the University of Central Florida, one of the largest universities in the nation by enrollment, with Valencia College students joining too. Nearby Winter Park has its own Chabad for the smaller, close-knit Rollins College community.',
  gulf:
    'On the Gulf Coast, Tampa has Chabad centers at both the University of South Florida and the University of Tampa, and Fort Myers welcomes students from Florida Gulf Coast University and Florida SouthWestern.',
  south:
    'South Florida has the densest Jewish community in the state, and its campuses reflect it: two Chabad centers at the University of Miami, plus Chabad at FIU, Miami Dade College, Nova Southeastern and Florida Atlantic University in Boca Raton, which also serves Lynn University and Palm Beach State.',
};
const ld = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    name: 'Florida colleges and universities with Chabad on Campus',
    itemListElement: colleges.map((r, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: r.campus.name, url: `${SITE.url}${r.center.url}${r.campus.primary ? '' : '#' + r.campus.anchor}` })),
  },
];
---
<Guide
  title="Jewish life at Florida colleges and universities"
  metaTitle="Jewish Life at Florida Colleges & Universities"
  description={`Jewish life at Florida universities, region by region: ${stats.campuses} colleges served by ${stats.centers} Chabad on Campus centers, estimated Jewish student populations, kosher food and Shabbat.`}
  path={path}
  lead={`Florida has one of the largest Jewish communities in the country, and Jewish students will find Chabad on Campus at ${stats.campuses} colleges and universities across the state. Here is where, region by region.`}
  image="florida-pegisha-students"
  imageAlt="Jewish students from Florida colleges together at the Florida Regional Pegisha Shabbaton"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Jewish Life on Campus', href: '/jewish-life-on-campus/' }, { name: 'Florida', href: path }]}
  jsonLd={ld}
  wide
>
  <p>Whether you are choosing a college or already enrolled, it helps to know what Jewish life looks like across Florida. The state has large public flagships with thousands of Jewish students, mid-size universities where Jewish community is close-knit, and private colleges where the Chabad House may be the center of Jewish life on campus. Every school below has a Chabad on Campus center nearby, and every one of them hosts Shabbat dinners and celebrates the Jewish holidays with students.</p>

  <h2>Florida universities with the largest Jewish student populations</h2>
  <p>These estimates are reported by Chabad on Campus International and include undergraduate and graduate students. They are approximate, but they give a sense of scale.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">University</th><th scope="col">Estimated Jewish students</th><th scope="col">Chabad center</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {biggest.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={r.campus.primary ? r.center.url : `${r.center.url}#${r.campus.anchor}`}>{r.campus.name}</a></td>
            <td>{formatNumber(r.campus.jewishStudents!)}</td>
            <td>{r.center.officialName}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  {regions.map((r) => (
    <section class="region">
      <h2>Jewish life in {r.name}</h2>
      <p>{regionCopy[r.region]}</p>
      <div class="rgrid">
        {r.centers.map((c) => {
          const kosher = c.amenities.filter((a) => KOSHER_KEYS.includes(a.key)).length > 0;
          return (
            <div class="rcard">
              <h3><a href={c.url}>Jewish life at {withThe(c.primaryCampus.name)}</a></h3>
              <p class="small muted">{c.officialName} &middot; {c.city}</p>
              <ul>
                {c.primaryCampus.jewishStudents && <li>About {formatNumber(c.primaryCampus.jewishStudents)} Jewish students</li>}
                {c.otherCampuses.length > 0 && <li>Also serves {c.otherCampuses.map((o) => o.abbr || o.name).join(', ')}</li>}
                {kosher && <li>Kosher food options</li>}
                {c.programs.some((p) => p.program.slug === 'jewishu' && p.confirmed) && <li>JewishU courses</li>}
                {c.programs.some((p) => p.program.slug === 'sinai-scholars' && p.confirmed) && <li>Sinai Scholars Society</li>}
              </ul>
            </div>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Every Florida college with Chabad on Campus</h2>
  <p>Some Chabad Houses serve several nearby schools. If your college is on this list, there is a Chabad House ready to welcome you.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">College or university</th><th scope="col">Chabad center</th><th scope="col">City</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {colleges.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={r.campus.primary ? r.center.url : `${r.center.url}#${r.campus.anchor}`}>{r.campus.name}</a>{r.campus.abbr && <span class="muted"> ({r.campus.abbr})</span>}</td>
            <td><a href={r.center.url}>{r.center.officialName}</a></td>
            <td>{r.center.city}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Beyond your own campus</h2>
  <p>Florida's Chabad centers also bring students together across the state. The <a href="/programs/pegisha/">Florida Regional Pegisha</a> Shabbaton gathers students from many Florida schools for a weekend, and students from every center can join <a href="/programs/birthright-israel/">Birthright Israel with Chabad</a>, <a href="/programs/living-links/">Living Links</a> and the <a href="/programs/study-away-grant/">Study Away Grant</a>. If you are still choosing a school, read <a href="/jewish-life-on-campus/choosing-a-college/">how to choose a college with Jewish life</a>.</p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .region { margin-top: 12px; }
  .rgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin: 16px 0 8px; }
  .rcard { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px; }
  .rcard h3 { font-size: 1.02rem; margin: 0 0 2px; }
  .rcard h3 a { text-decoration: none; }
  .rcard p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .rcard ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1em; font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
